  "details": "Feature Request:\n\nWould like the ability to be able to lock the 3rd person camera after repositioning it to the desired position in order to re-enable mouse control over avatar head movements.\n\nCurrent behavior prioritizes camera movements meaning that avatar head movements can now only be done via selfie expressions which in turns takes away one of the methods that desktop users use to communicate.\n\n----\n\nBug:\n\nThere also seems to be a slight bug in that after leaving fly mode, control over the avatar's head does not return to the mouse until the user toggles between first and third person again. \n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nEnter 3rd person view\n\nPress tab to enter fly mode\n\nPress tab again to disable fly mode\n\nHead movements are no longer controllable by mouse\n\nZoom in to first person mode\n\nZoom out to third person mode\n\nHead movements are now controllable by mouse",
